This is the comp at **1 s**, halfway through Title's first move. Title should be the faint "An easing lesson" text. It's still fading in here.

Right now, between 0.5 s and 1.5 s, Title's Position, Scale and Opacity all change at a **constant speed**. They start at full speed and then stop dead. Position then sets off again at a constant speed until 3 s. That's why it feels mechanical. Easing makes the motion slow down as it reaches each keyframe and speed up as it leaves.

**How to ease a pair:**
1. Select Title and press **U** to show its keyframes.
2. Select both keys of a pair.
3. Choose **Animation > Keyframe Assistant > Easy Ease**, or press **F9**.

The diamond keyframes turn into hourglass shapes. To see the curve, open the **Graph Editor** (the graph icon above the timeline). A straight line becomes a smooth S-shape.

**The 4 pairs on Title:**
- Position, 0.5 s → 1.5 s
- Position, 1.5 s → 3 s
- Scale, 0.5 s → 1.5 s
- Opacity, 0.5 s → 1.5 s

